      "why": "Line 9 sets signal to AbortSignal.timeout(TIMEOUT_MS), with TIMEOUT_MS set to 5000 on line 1, so the fetch aborts after 5 s. The catch on lines 13-15 returns status PENDING for a TimeoutError or any other error. The behaviour is built.",
      "verdict": "built"
     },
     {
      "id": "DEC-02",
      "path": "src/refund-service.js",
      "line": 13,
      "why": "Line 13 returns the stored result when the order is already in the store, so a repeat refund is not sent again. The store is read on line 13 and written on line 15, both before the gateway call on line 16, so a store that throws stops the refund before anything is sent. The behaviour is built.",
      "verdict": "built"
     }
    ]
   },
